  "title": "Titusville Leans on CAD-to-CAD During Historic Floods",
  "summary": "When unprecedented flooding impacted Titusville, Florida, the Titusville Police Department Communications Center managed a significant surge in emergency calls while coordinating response efforts across the city. Over the course of five hours, the communications center received approximately 452 calls for service, including 213 calls into 911. Many of the incidents involved people trapped inside vehicles as floodwater quickly rose throughout the city. In some areas, vehicles drifted...",
